    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a clear core of offensive anchors, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.39), and **Kyle Tucker** (71.13). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier start, benefiting from a highly favorable matchup against Pecko, whose 5.95 xERA is the softest on the board; the combination of a high-value third-spot order assignment and a dynamic platoon advantage makes him the engine of today\u2019s lineup. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** maintains a high floor despite a slight negative platoon adjustment, as his matchup against Lugo, S presents a strong opportunity for run production. Even with a tough draw against Elder, **Kyle Tucker** remains locked in as an elite play, as his raw base projection and strong park factors keep his efficiency score well within our top tier.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Miguel Vargas**, who landed just shy of our threshold at 39.33, effectively falling into the bench bucket to preserve our game caps. While his xwOBA remains competitive at 0.389, the combination of facing a tier-one arm in deGrom and being forced to contend with an elite hold (50% SB suppression) made him a clear \"sit\" compared to our active starters. We are monitoring the status of several bench pieces like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Heliot Ramos**, who remain unavailable due to injury or depth chart shifts, leaving us with a condensed bench. \n\nRisks are heavily concentrated in our middle infield and outfield, where **Nasim Nunez** and **Jackson Merrill** face significant defensive hurdles. **Nasim Nunez** draws an elite arm in Adams (2.25 xERA), and while his versatility is noted, his low order placement further depresses his score. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Robert Jr.** are battling negative platoon adjustments and aggressive stolen base suppression from their respective opposing catchers, which severely limits their ceiling in our scarcest category. We are proceeding with **Liam Hicks** and **Coby Mayo** in the lineup, both of whom provide necessary stability, though we will be watching for mid-game adjustments should weather or early pitching dominance threaten these thin margins.",
